# Java imports and type names

Prefer an `import` and the simple type name. Do not use fully qualified names (FQN) in type references (`implements`, `extends`, fields, parameters, casts, `new`, etc.) unless there is a name conflict.

```java
// BAD
public class ReportDataManager implements com.yukthitech.autox.exec.IReportDataManager

// GOOD
import com.yukthitech.autox.exec.IReportDataManager;
public class ReportDataManager implements IReportDataManager
```

Use FQN only when two types share the same simple name and both are needed in the same file (e.g. `java.util.Date` vs `java.sql.Date`). In that case, import one and FQN the other, or FQN both for clarity.
